{"id": "q0017", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 738267562, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Madeline ate 6 grapes. Her brother wanted to make grape juice and used up 5 times as many grapes then Madeline to make a full glass. Their mother then used the remaining grapes to make 4 pies. How many grapes were there at the beginning if the pie recipe calls for 12 grapes per pie?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0017.wav", "input_sha256": "ffe89c2760460375b94b2dea8e2f9800dd0cff9d8a600e2ee2b36f8f615811a7", "input_samples": 350200, "input_s": 21.887, "n_real_chunks": 22, "score": 0.1666, "act": 0.9986, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "So Madeline ate six grapes. Her brother used five times as many to make grape juice, so that's 5 times 6, which is 30 gra pes for the juice. Their mother made four pies, and each pie uses 12 grapes, so 4 times 12 is 4 8 gra pes for the pies. Now, adding all those up: 6 plus 3 0 plus 4 8 equal s 84 gra pes in total. So there were 8 4 grapes at the beginning.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 22, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 28, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0017_local_local.wav", "sha256": "5cb27fad45d6137a1c4b1545cf33f78fad60fb858a2f40b74b86af8ee9e24749", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 28.2}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.082, 1.148, 1, 0, 0