{"id": "q0091", "pool": "frozen", "arm": "local", "tier": "never", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 230375063, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "923cbbdfe3213927dfa36b1f8e0eb48a30d641d9b9bf7cf25d16765340d88836", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": null, "gpu": "NVIDIA H100 80GB HBM3", "host": "modal", "shard": 6, "query": "Aaron and Vanessa were relay race partners on a running team. Aaron was able to run each mile twice as fast as Vanessa, but Vanessa was able to run twice as far as Aaron did. If Vanessa ran 4 miles and Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, how long in minutes did Vanessa take to complete her part?\n\nShow your work and end with the final numeric answer.", "input_path": "/data/audio_pool/q0091.wav", "input_sha256": "c9d30e32f0e214f9a7dea809ed5fa76c96786c710fb1e04c79f4c5680a2736cc", "input_samples": 372000, "input_s": 23.25, "n_real_chunks": 24, "score": 0.2297, "act": 0.9993, "is_info": true, "fired": false, "mode": "local", "answer": "Vanessa ran 4 miles, so Aaron ran half of that or 2 miles. If Aaron completed his part of the race in 16 minutes, then Vanessa took twice as long to run her distance, which would be 32 minutes. The answer is 3 2.", "relay_text": "", "expert_answer": "", "transcript": "", "asr_s": null, "expert_s": null, "expert_input_samples": null, "expert_input_s": null, "expert_input_sha256": null, "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": null, "relay_synth_ms": null, "onset_chunk": 23, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 14, "feed_lag_max_ms": 0, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 0, "audio_files": {"local": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/frozen/audio/q0091_local_local.wav", "sha256": "eaca978bcebf78e8dbdf331a2e51e998da82eed0ec68d3fe776678084e7bed69", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 14.28}}, "chunks": [[0, 1, 1.0, 1.061, 1.11, 1, 0, 0], [1, 1, 2.0, 2.067, 2.121, 1, 0, 0], [2, 1, 3.0, 3.069, 3.121, 1, 0, 0], [3, 1, 4.0, 4.069, 4.123, 1, 0, 0], [4, 1, 5